__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Claude Code's per-repo working directory. Today this holds NOTHING BUT
# `worktrees/` -- git worktrees nested inside the repo itself, one per parallel
# session, each a full checkout with its own `.git` file. Untracked, they show
# up as a permanent `?? .claude/` in every `git status` and are one `git add -A`
# away from being swept in, which is the same failure mode the vendor-material
# rules above already guard against.
#
# SCOPED TO THE TRANSIENT PARTS, not to `.claude/` wholesale, deliberately:
# `.claude/settings.json`, `.claude/agents/` and `.claude/skills/` are shared
# project configuration that a team may well WANT tracked, and a blanket
# `.claude/` would silently ignore them the day someone adds one. What is
# ignored here is what is machine-local by nature -- a worktree belongs to one
# checkout on one host, and `settings.local.json` is per-user by Claude Code's
# own convention.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# The deployment's own settings: `github.repo`, the budget, the model, whatever this
# checkout overrides in the tracked `configs/WORKFLOW.md`. Machine-local by nature,
# like the worktrees above: one checkout watches one repository, and tracking the file
# would put that repository's name in issuebot's own history and make every `git pull`
# a merge on the one file the operator has rewritten. `*.local.md` rather than the one
# name so a second workflow file on a host (`--workflow frontend.md`) has its
# `frontend.local.md` ignored too.
configs/*.local.md

# Local secrets - service principal creds for the FOCUS export storage account.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Superpowers SDD scratch: ledger, task briefs, implementer reports and review
# packages for a plan being executed. Machine-local and per-run by nature, and
# regenerated from the plan file, so it is never worth tracking. Same reasoning
# as `.claude/worktrees/` above -- untracked it would sit in every `git status`
# one `git add -A` away from being swept into a commit.
.superpowers/
